goodsServices.description:
(1) Testing to determine professional competency in the field of deafblind intervention; promoting the interests of certified deafblind intervenors in the field of deafblind intervention; maintaining a registry of certified professionals in the field of deafblind intervention 
(2) Development of intervenor standards, namely, professional standards and best practices in the field of personal support for deafblind individuals; developing, administering and evaluating qualifying educational examination for certification purposes in the field of deaf blindness deafblind intervenor profession 
(3) Research in the field of deaf blindness; analysis and evaluation of deafblind intervention services of others to determine conformity with accreditation and certification standards through the assessment and evaluation of intervenor education, knowledge, and experience in the field of deafblind intervention;

